This project independently maintains NixOS integration for OnePlus Pad 2 Pro.

Current device dependencies:
- linux-sm8750-erhai-patchset, mirrored in inputs/kernel-patchset/ with its
  manifest, original patch authorship, licenses and provenance. Official Linux
  is fetched through nixpkgs; Linux driver notices remain unchanged.
- kShimC-oneplus-pad2-pro, mirrored in inputs/kshim-protocol/. Its source.json
  pins the upstream revision, local publisher extension and effective hashes.

Locally maintained audio sources in packages/audio/ were imported from
https://github.com/yzddmr6/onepluspad-2pro-mainline revision
4cc3570c7c14689d77e58c081d2430170288f72a (BSD-3-Clause). The board topology,
TDM/MFC helpers and UCM no longer require fetching that project. The bundled
linux-msm/audioreach-topology archive is revision
993a17dcb672357998a463a73f120064d6c74f4f; its BSD license and source manifest
are installed with the package. NixOS uses amplifier level 270 (-22.5 dB).
The WirePlumber speaker volume rule was adapted from the same source's
MIT-licensed 51-erhai-speaker.conf.

Firmware provenance is maintained in inputs/firmware/. The original base
inventory was imported from the same device-source revision; its source and
license notices remain in ORIGINAL-NOTICES.md. Wi-Fi and Bluetooth inventories
were initially verified using ArmadaOS's OPD2413 records, revision
937d88a2c28a67153d572bcf7f89049eaada93f2. These are provenance references,
not build or runtime dependencies. Firmware archives are bundled as ordinary Git files under inputs/firmware/archives/
and retain their original vendor licenses. They are not relicensed under the kernel GPL.
No per-unit factory data, addresses or pairing keys are included in Git.

Historical frozen kernel configurations and patches are retained under
docs/history/kernel/ and do not participate in current builds.

tools/bluetooth-address.py and tests/test_bluetooth_address.py are adapted
from ArmadaOS devices/oneplus-pad2pro/rootfs/overlay/usr/libexec/armada/
opd2413-btaddr and tests/test_btaddr.py (MIT). The NixOS service supplies
the tablet's separately provisioned factory public address before BlueZ
starts. Per-device identity stays in /var/lib/oneplus-pad2pro/bt-address,
outside the Nix store, and is not generated or shared between devices.

Automatic OPD2413 factory identity extraction (tools/bluetooth_factory.py)
and the direct Linux MGMT client (tools/bluetooth_mgmt.py) are MIT licensed.
The factory record format and address byte order were independently verified
against this tablet's Android 16 nvram_server, nvram_qmi and Bluetooth HAL.
No proprietary Android code, binaries, device serials or factory records
are included. The decoder reads and validates the unit's own nonmodemst1/2
partitions; the per-device address is recovered at runtime, not built into
the package. Python cryptography retains its upstream licenses.

kShimC external boot protocol and inputs/kshim-protocol/boot_files.py:
https://github.com/ZEGEIZI/kShimC-oneplus-pad2-pro
Revision: 471c93186579566bf135fed0b34caa632b1da115.
The local optional payload-sharing extension is recorded in
inputs/kshim-protocol/patches/shared-payloads.patch. The runtime boot protocol
is unchanged; the source license is in inputs/kshim-protocol/LICENSE.

The source references below describe historical imports; the imported code is
maintained locally or in the independent device patchset.

Adreno 830 Mesa patches in packages/mesa/ are imported unchanged from
onepluspad-2pro-mainline revision 4cc3570c7c14689d77e58c081d2430170288f72a,
packaging/mesa/shared/mesa/. The original source manifest is preserved as
upstream-source.json, including SHA-256 digests and upstream attribution.
These patches are MIT licensed; original patch authorship notices remain.
Mesa itself is fetched by nixpkgs and retains its upstream licenses.

Opt-in DPU 8-bpc output dithering in docs/history/kernel/patches/dpu-xn242-8bpc-dither.patch
is adapted from ArmadaOS patch 0049-drm-msm-dpu-panel-opt-in-8bpc-dither.patch,
by enjihn <150061999+enjihn@users.noreply.github.com>, at ArmadaOS revision
937d88a2c28a67153d572bcf7f89049eaada93f2. The original Linux DRM GPL-2.0 notices remain; the opt-in
property is renamed to qcom,dpu-8bpc-dither for distribution independence.
This patch does not include Lenovo-specific 10-bpc panel initialization or
advertise BT.2100/PQ support on the OnePlus panel.

OPD2413 OEM Bluetooth bootstrap and UART handling are adapted in the shared
linux-sm8750-erhai tree from ArmadaOS reference 937d88a2c28a67153d572bcf7f89049eaada93f2,
devices/oneplus-pad2pro/kernel/current/final-modules (GPL-2.0-only).
docs/history/kernel/patches/opd2413-brahma-bluetooth.patch exports its driver and DT
runtime changes against the historical frozen source; the adjacent source manifest
records the port and shared file hashes. Existing driver notices remain.
OEM Bluetooth binaries are separate bundled proprietary archives, pinned
by inputs/firmware/bluetooth.json; no redistribution grant is implied.
Factory identity and pairing keys are excluded.
